Boots require *two* turns to put on/off. Being burdened or worse, or
putting on/off multiple items in one go via A-command, prolongs that
time.

During dressing, you are basically "helpless" and a present Elbereth
does NOT protect you. That's why one can die "...while dressing up".

It's like engraving with a hard gem, where an existing Elbereth does
not protect one either until the new (added) engraving is completely
finished.

So... Putting on your speed boots made you helpless, allowing the long
worm to attack you, because Elbereth had no effect during the dressing
phase. After you had finished dressing, you were not helpless anymore,
Elbereth protection kicked in again and scared the worm normally.

